    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d94">

                <pb facs="0201" n="163" sameAs="frus:frus1951v03p1/pg163"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.5/5–2451: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The United States Deputy Representative on the North
                        Atlantic Council</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Spofford</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-05-24T21:00:00+01:00">May 24, 1951—9 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    Depto 990. Re Todep 437,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d94-f1"/> believe it is neither
                    desirable nor advisable attempt define formally relationship between UN and
                    collective self-def orgs. Understand this question was subj of considerable
                    study during negot, signature and ratification NAT and that US Govt position then was that NAT was fully within framework UN charter and cld
                    be employed by UN in exercise its primary responsibility for maintenance
                    internatl peace and security. This seems to us to be simple expression which
                    makes clear that there is no conflict between NAT and UN charter, but does not establish formal relationship
                    between the two. We can see no reason for any modification this policy and on
                    other hand can see many possible difficulties in attempting further to define
                    formal relationship.</p>
                <pb facs="0202" n="164" xml:id="pg164"/>
                <p>We, therefore, recommend that US Govt not seek internatl acceptance of
                    “principles concerning the relationship between the UN and collective def and
                    regional orgs” embodied in reftel.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Spofford</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d94-f1" n="1" xml:id="d94-f1-content">
                <p>This telegram to London of May 18, not printed, requested comment on an enclosed
                    text entitled “Principles Governing the Relationship between the United Nations
                    and Collective Self-Defense and Regional Organizations” (396.1 ISG/5–1851).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
